.env
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
logs/*.log
logs/*.csv
data/*.csv
data/session_state.json
data/ai_call_budget.json
data/news_audit_log.jsonl
data/news_high_priority.jsonl
data/dashboard_token.txt

# Exchange session cookies. Written by the nse/bse libraries on every
# run, rotate constantly, and are session state -- not source. Committed
# by accident on 2026-07-27 (data/nse_cookies_requests.json).
data/*cookies*.json

# Scratch files from live investigation -- downloaded filings, one-off
# snapshots. Regenerable, sometimes many MB, never source.
data/_test_*.pdf
# tests/fixtures/*.txt are the extracted TEXT of real filings -- small,
# committed on purpose, so the 7 MB PDFs never need to be.
data/bse_lag_snapshot_*.json

# Databases (regenerated; keep the repo light)
data/*.db
data/*.db.bak_*
*.db-journal
data/entries_paused.flag
data/universe_review.csv
data/*.csv.gz
data/*.zip
data/filings/

# Telegram session -- a CREDENTIAL. Anyone holding this file can read
# the operator's Telegram account. Never commit it.
data/telegram_session.session
data/telegram_session*
data/telegram.db

# ---- Scratch files that got committed by a broad `git add`. ----
# 12 August 2026. All four were staged into the repo by accident:
# .c1/.c2 are two halves of a `ls tests/` dump, .__write_test is a
# zero-byte probe some code writes to check the disk is writable, and
# .suite.log was an empty pytest redirect. None is a source file.
.c1
.c2
.__write_test
.suite.log

# A malformed database path -- something built "sqlite:/data/..." as a
# literal directory instead of parsing the URL. The real store is
# data/stock_events.db.
sqlite:/

# ---- node_modules: 1,806 files, 26 MB, staged by accident. ----
# 12 August 2026. There is no package.json, so nothing recorded what
# these were or why. The only thing in there is a HALF-INSTALLED jsdom
# that tests/test_dom_sims_actually_run.py already documents as broken:
# "On 3 August it was found to HANG on require('jsdom') and get killed".
# Every tests/dom/*.sim.js was rewritten to use node builtins only, and
# all six pass with nothing installed.
#
# Untracked, not deleted -- the files stay on disk. Committing them was
# what left a `git add` running for two hours holding .git/index.lock.
node_modules/

# The Dhan access token the bot mints for itself (core/dhan_auth.py).
# A LIVE CREDENTIAL -- anyone holding it can trade the account until it
# expires, same class as the Telegram session below. Cached on disk from
# 13 August 2026 so a restart reuses the 24-hour token instead of asking
# Dhan for another and being rate-limited.
data/dhan_token.json

# Which main.py is alive, by pid (core/single_instance.py, 13 Aug 2026).
# Machine-local and meaningless anywhere else. Replaces the port probe
# that could not see a second bot on Windows.
data/main_bot.lock

# ---- WRITE-AHEAD SIDECARS AND BACKUPS. 14 August 2026. ----
# Found during the store inventory: data/*.db is ignored but sqlite's
# own -wal/-shm companions are not, and neither were the timestamped
# master_stocks backups the fixer tools leave behind. All regenerable,
# none of it source, and a -wal committed beside an ignored .db is a
# half-written database in the history.
data/*.db-wal
data/*.db-shm
data/*.csv.*.bak
data/*.csv.bak_*
data/telegram_reader.lock
data/preopen_history/
logs/*.log.[0-9]*

# Each stock's own intraday volume curve, rebuilt nightly by
# tools/build_volume_profile.py from data/history_candles.db. 8 MB and
# regenerated every night -- tracking it would add that much to the
# history daily. data/liquidity.json is tracked because it is 47 KB.
# core/volume_pace.py falls back to the whole-day ratio when it is
# missing, and nightly's health step reports a stale store.
data/volume_profile.json

# Database backups written by tools/dedupe_events.py before it removes
# anything. 11 MB each and regenerated on demand -- kept on disk so a
# removed row is always recoverable by id, never in git history.
data/*.db.*.bak
